---
description: Engine choice and the React/Phaser boundary
alwaysApply: true
---

- The gameplay engine is **Phaser 3 + TypeScript**. Do not introduce another
  renderer (PixiJS, DOM animation libs, canvas hand-rolling) for gameplay.
- React is only the shell: landing, lobby, room create/join, multiplayer
  connection, game-over, debug panel, small HUD chips. React must never
  render in-round gameplay visuals.
- The only boundary between React/network and Phaser is
  `client/src/game/GameEventBridge.ts`. Network pushes state in; the scene
  emits player intents out. Do not import scene internals from React or vice
  versa.
- `PhaserGame.tsx` owns only canvas lifecycle (mount/destroy). Game state
  never lives in React component state.
- The rationale is documented in `docs/GAME_ENGINE_DECISION.md`; update it if
  the engine decision ever changes.
